# Phase 10c.3: waiver list for the image-scan gate in .github/workflows/ci.yml (the e2e job's
# "Scan backend/frontend image for vulnerabilities" steps). Same shape as
# .github/scripts/npm-audit-gate.mjs's ALLOWLIST: everything not listed here at HIGH/CRITICAL fails
# the build, and everything listed here is a decision, not an oversight. Trivy reads the `exp:` date
# on each line itself and stops honouring the entry once it passes, so an expired waiver goes back to
# failing the build rather than waiving silently forever.
#
# Backend image scanned clean at HIGH/CRITICAL when this file was written (2026-08-18) - nothing to
# list for it. Everything below is the frontend image.
#
# Re-scanned 2026-10-03 with Trivy 0.74.0 (`trivy image --severity CRITICAL,HIGH --ignore-unfixed`,
# this file not applied). The rebuilt frontend image (next 16.3.8 on
# node:26-alpine@sha256:0b36e8c136b94cd4fcf02188228e76c31ad5872eef3fec8cbd2eee500cfd9e80)
# reports exactly the three CVEs below. An earlier scan of the previous image (next 16.3.3 on
# node:26-alpine@sha256:aadf416b…) is what surfaced the next advisory that was then bumped.
#
# Dropped, because that scan no longer reports them:
# - The vendored-in-next block (tar/cross-spawn/postcss under next/dist/compiled) was already gone
#   on 2026-09-04 and is still gone. postcss and sharp in the app tree are clean.
# - next itself was NOT clean: GHSA-vcvr-r3jv-pc5j, a critical RCE in next/og ImageResponse, on
#   16.3.3, fixed in 16.3.6. That is an app dependency, so it was bumped to next@16.3.8 instead of
#   waived.
# - Bundled-npm CVEs that npm 11.19.1 in the new digest no longer carries: CVE-2026-14257,
#   CVE-2026-69152, CVE-2026-69192, CVE-2026-73566.
# - CVE-2026-14456 (OpenSSL QUIC server DoS). The new digest has libssl3/libcrypto3 3.5.8-r0, which
#   is the fixed package. CVE-2026-45447 was already absent on the previous digest.

# The base image's own global npm install (/usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/node_modules/*), not a
# dependency of this app. The container's CMD is `node server.js`, which never shells out to npm,
# so these copies are not on a request path. Not fixable from this repo: they move only when the
# base image ships a newer bundled npm. npm in this digest is 11.19.1.
#
# brace-expansion 5.0.9: DoS via stack exhaustion (CVE-2026-102276, fixed in 5.0.10) and via
# nested-brace recursion (CVE-2026-102278, fixed in 5.0.11).
# undici 6.28.0: DoS via an unrequested WebSocket subprotocol (CVE-2026-19534, fixed in 6.28.1).
CVE-2026-102276 exp:2026-12-02
CVE-2026-102278 exp:2026-12-02
CVE-2026-19534 exp:2026-12-02
